package api

import (
	"fmt"
	"net/http"

	"github.com/sjawhar/envoy/internal/contracts"
	"github.com/sjawhar/envoy/internal/dispatch/model"
)

var _ = declareRoute(routeDecl{
	Method:      http.MethodPatch,
	Pattern:     "/api/v1/issues/{key}",
	Auth:        authAny,
	Description: fmt.Sprintf("Update title (over %d characters is 400 CAP_EXCEEDED), status, priority, labels (or labels_add, which adds to the labels the issue holds when the write commits rather than replacing them; not with labels), route, parent, rank, assignee (the email of a person who has signed in, or null; anyone may reassign), advances, or components ({mode: inherit|explicit|none, ids, reason}; allowed on a closed issue). A priority of 0 needs the p0 scope when the write makes the issue's own priority 0, from none or from another value: from a credential that does not hold p0 it is 403 OAUTH_SCOPE_REQUIRED naming p0, under a WWW-Authenticate challenge for p0, before every refusal that reads the issue (409 ISSUE_CHANGED and 409 ISSUE_CLOSED among them), and writes no field of the issue and no event of it. For a close that names priority 0 from a credential without p0, the PATCH reads the issue's own priority first, and where it is not 0 it refuses the close before it settles the issue's documents; a close whose own priority moves away from 0 between that read and the owner's lock can settle the documents and is then refused. A person at a browser holds p0, a personal token holds it only where its maker gave it, and a write that keeps priority 0 on an issue that holds it, lowers it, clears it or sets 1 to 3 needs no scope; a priority that an issue above the issue has is none of its own. advances is the issue's whole list of its own priorities, which replaces the list it holds ([] clears it; an inherited entry is no relation of the issue and no write states or retracts one): more than %d ids, counted before duplicates are removed, an id no priority carries, and one whose priority is gone are each 400 ADVANCES_INPUT. advances_revision is the advances_revision of the issue read the write answers: a write whose advances_revision is not the revision the issue holds is 409 ADVANCES_REVISION naming the one it holds, and a write that names no revision may assert or retract one relation, so one that would change two or more is 409 ADVANCES_REVISION too, naming the revision held. A closed issue refuses advances (409 ISSUE_CLOSED). Closing the issue (status done) withdraws every open ask it holds, each recorded resolved with resolution kind withdrawn naming the closer; reopening it opens exactly those asks again. expected_sequence makes the write conditional: 409 ISSUE_CHANGED when the issue's last event is no longer that sequence. With DISPATCH_PARENT_STATUS_RULE on, a status or a parent that would leave a parent out of line with its children is 409 PARENT_STATUS_CONFLICT {code, error, issues: [{key, title, status, relation}]}, relation parent or child, issues naming each issue that holds the rule. issues and error leave out an issue of a private project that the request's credential does not name, so issues can be empty. refuse_open_foreign_children, beside a status of retro or done, asks for the check of an acceptance write, and with any other status or none it is 400 INVALID_ISSUE. While the issue has a child of another project in any status but done and icebox, such a write is 409 FOREIGN_CHILD_OPEN {code, error, issues: [{key, project, status}]}, the children in key order, after the parent status rule. issues and error leave out a child of a private project that the request's credential does not name, so issues can be empty, and the write is refused all the same. With DISPATCH_LEGION_STATUS_SCOPE on, three writes of a Legion issue need a credential that holds the person scope or legion-status. A Legion issue carries the legion label in any case, or is under an issue of its own project that does. The three writes are a status write (the status the issue holds included) where the issue is a Legion issue before the call or after it, the removal of its legion label, and a move after which it is no longer a Legion issue (a move out from under every labelled issue). A credential that holds neither scope is 403 LEGION_STATUS_SCOPE_REQUIRED for each, with an insufficient_scope challenge naming legion-status, and the call writes no field of the issue and no event of it; a refused close (status done) can still settle the issue's documents, which the PATCH does before it judges the write. The one exception is the owning architect's status write: a broker-issued token whose session the Legion daemon's own token published as the architect of an issue above the issue, of the issue's own project, before the call and after it, writes the status done, backlog, icebox or triage, while the removal of the label and the move stay refused to it. On an issue Legion runs, a close, a reopen and a labels or parent write that takes the issue out of Legion are 403 DOCUMENT_WRITER_NOT_ARCHITECT from a session that is no person, no architect of the issue or of an issue above it, and not the session of the project's Legion daemon. A move under a parent, after which Legion runs the issue, is 403 DOCUMENT_WRITER_NOT_ARCHITECT from a session that is no person and no architect of the new parent or of an issue above it. A move under a parent of another project is judged as a root of the issue's own project, which this check does not judge. When Legion runs the issue, or an issue under it, before the move, the move is 403 DOCUMENT_WRITER_NOT_ARCHITECT too, wherever the new parent is, from a session that is no person and no architect of each such issue or of an issue above it where it stands: the issue itself when Legion runs it, and else each issue under it with the label legion that it reaches through parents of its own project. An issue's chain ends at the first parent of another project, as at a root. Neither check of a move passes the session of the project's Legion daemon.", contracts.IssueTitleMax, contracts.MaxIssueAdvances),
	Handler:     (*server).patchIssue,
	Successor:   successorIs(http.MethodPatch, "/issues/{key}"),
	WriteClass:  scopeProject,
	Shape: routeShape{
		Status: http.StatusOK, Response: model.Issue{}, Request: updateIssueInput{}, Advice: writeAdvice{},
		Refusals: []routeAnswer{
			// An acceptance write that asks for the open-child check (refuse_open_foreign_children)
			// over an open child of another project (refuseOpenForeignChildren).
			{Status: http.StatusConflict, Body: foreignChildOpenError{}},
			// With DISPATCH_PARENT_STATUS_RULE on, a status or a parent that breaks the rule.
			{Status: http.StatusConflict, Body: parentStatusConflictBody{}},
		},
	},
})
